ℹ️ Île Sainte-Hélène is the northern island of Parc Jean-Drapeau, a natural island in the St. Lawrence River that was expanded with rock excavated from the Montréal Metro for Expo 67. The post highlights it for its gardens, picnic spots, nature trails, and some of the best views of Montréal's skyline.</description>
